#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0127 expect=violation domain=SE
#note "POLARITY PIN, firing direction (Fix #284 / M3-D1). Subject 001's LAST Subject Element is SESEQ=2, so is_last_in_group(group=[USUBJID], by=SESEQ) is true on row 2 only. Its SEENDTC is 2020-01-20 while the subject disposition date DS.DSSTDTC is 2020-01-15, so the two DIFFER -- exactly the state the Description (\"does not equal\"), the Outcome Message (\"does not equal\") and the sheet Rule (SEENDTC = DS.DSSTDTC of the disposition, i.e. the CONFORMANT state) say the rule reports. The shipped Check compared with == and was therefore silent here and loud on every conforming subject; M3-D1 changes it to !=. Row 1 (SESEQ=1) is not the last element so is_last_in_group is false there and it cannot contribute -- hence exactly one finding. NOT the Fix #158 repair: CDISC-SEND-0283's sheet Rule cell says 'must immediately precede or be the same as' and took date_greater_than; row 630's cell here is an exact equality and takes !=."
#library standard=sendig version=3-0
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 USUBJID=001 SESEQ=2
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
col SEENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | 001 | 1 | SCRN | 2020-01-01 | 2020-01-10
S1 | SE | 001 | 2 | TRT | 2020-01-10 | 2020-01-20
---

dataset DS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
col DSSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Disposition Event"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | TERMINAL SACRIFICE | 2020-01-15
---
